<title>USA: 3M Pharmaceuticals to market treatment.</title>
<headline>3M Pharmaceuticals to market treatment.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>3M Pharmaceuticals Inc said Monday it received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market Aldara cream to treat external genital warts, a sexually transmitted disease.</p>
<p>3M Pharmaceuticals is a unit of Minnesota Mining &amp; Manufacturing Co.</p>
<p>Aldara is the newest in a class of drug called immune response modifiers and represents the first new therapeutical approach to genital warts in five years, the company said in a statement.  Aldara will be available by prescription only.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
